# Augment Guidelines for rippled Project

## Sub-Agent Rules

### Build Serialization

**CRITICAL: Only run ONE build at a time across all sub-agents.**

- Do NOT run parallel builds from multiple sub-agents simultaneously
- If delegating work to sub-agents, only ONE sub-agent should build at a time
- Other sub-agents should wait or do non-build work (analysis, code generation)
- Builds compete for CPU, memory, and ccache - parallel builds cause:
  - Resource contention and slower overall build times
  - ccache lock conflicts
  - Potential build failures from resource exhaustion

**Correct patterns for parallel sub-agents:**

**Option 1: Sequential builds (simple)**
1. Sub-agent A: Generate code, then build and verify
2. Sub-agent B: Generate code, wait for A to finish building, then build
3. OR: One sub-agent does all building after others complete code generation

**Option 2: Parallel builds on separate machines (preferred for testing multiple tasks)**
1. Sub-agent A: Build locally in `.build/`
2. Sub-agent B: Sync code to Azure TEE VM and build there

This allows true parallel testing without resource conflicts.

### Azure TEE VM for Parallel Builds

When testing multiple tasks simultaneously, use the Azure TEE VM (same machines used for distcc) as a separate build environment.

#### Syncing Code to Azure VM

```bash
# Sync the entire project to Azure VM (use any of the distcc hosts)
rsync -avz --exclude='.build' --exclude='.git/objects' \
    /home/edesouza/Projects/rippled/ \
    edesouza@10.100.1.17:/home/edesouza/Projects/rippled-test/

# Or use a specific test branch/directory name
rsync -avz --exclude='.build' --exclude='.git/objects' \
    /home/edesouza/Projects/rippled/ \
    edesouza@10.100.1.17:/home/edesouza/Projects/rippled-task-3-6/
```

#### Building on Azure VM

```bash
# SSH to the VM and build
ssh edesouza@10.100.1.17 "cd /home/edesouza/Projects/rippled-test/.build && ninja -j4 > build.log 2>&1"

# Check build results
ssh edesouza@10.100.1.17 "tail -50 /home/edesouza/Projects/rippled-test/.build/build.log"

# Check for errors
ssh edesouza@10.100.1.17 "grep -i 'error:' /home/edesouza/Projects/rippled-test/.build/build.log | head -20"
```

#### Initial Setup on Azure VM (one-time)

If the VM doesn't have a build directory configured:
```bash
ssh edesouza@10.100.1.17 << 'EOF'
cd /home/edesouza/Projects/rippled-test
mkdir -p .build && cd .build
cmake .. -G Ninja \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
    -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache \
    -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache
EOF
```

